From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arttttt <artem-bambalov@yandex.ru>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 03:10:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] recents: the screenshot goes after a frame shows the
 snapshot

Going home from overview with the home key cancels the recents
animation with the tasks' snapshots, and the system shows them in the
running task's place until the launcher calls cleanupScreenshot(). The
swipe handler called it at once, before the running task view had drawn
a snapshot: for one to four frames the view's live tile hole was on
screen, and the card blinked out and back in before fading. Whether it
blinked depended on the launcher's next frame winning that race.

Switch the running task view to the snapshots first and clean the
screenshot up once a frame with them is drawn, as the swipe-to-home
path already does with switchToScreenshot(); with a bound, so that a
frame that never comes cannot leave the system's screenshot up.
---
 quickstep/src/com/android/quickstep/AbsSwipeUpHandler.java | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/quickstep/src/com/android/quickstep/AbsSwipeUpHandler.java b/quickstep/src/com/android/quickstep/AbsSwipeUpHandler.java
--- a/quickstep/src/com/android/quickstep/AbsSwipeUpHandler.java
+++ b/quickstep/src/com/android/quickstep/AbsSwipeUpHandler.java
@@ -426,10 +426,26 @@
                 HashMap<Integer, ThumbnailData> snapshots =
                         mGestureState.consumeRecentsAnimationCanceledSnapshot();
                 if (snapshots != null) {
-                    mRecentsView.onRecentsAnimationComplete();
-                    if (mRecentsAnimationController != null) {
-                        mRecentsAnimationController.cleanupScreenshot();
-                    }
+                    // The system shows these snapshots in the task's place only until
+                    // cleanupScreenshot(). Taken away before the running task view has drawn
+                    // one of them, the view's live tile hole is on screen for a frame or more
+                    // and the card blinks out. So the view switches to the snapshots first,
+                    // and the screenshot goes once a frame with them is drawn -- or after a
+                    // bound, should no frame come.
+                    final RecentsAnimationController controller = mRecentsAnimationController;
+                    final boolean[] finished = {false};
+                    final Runnable finish = () -> {
+                        if (finished[0]) {
+                            return;
+                        }
+                        finished[0] = true;
+                        mRecentsView.onRecentsAnimationComplete();
+                        if (controller != null) {
+                            controller.cleanupScreenshot();
+                        }
+                    };
+                    mRecentsView.switchToScreenshot(snapshots, finish);
+                    MAIN_EXECUTOR.getHandler().postDelayed(finish, 200);
                 }
             });
 
